{
  "description": "How a transcript file loads: its bytes split on LF (0x0A) with empty pieces dropped, each piece read as transcript/lines.json pins and skipped when it does not decode; past 2000 decoded entries the file is rewritten with the newest 2000 (not reachable in this table: rust/powerup-core/src/transcript.rs load_tail_compacts_past_2000 and TranscriptStoreTests.testOvergrownFileIsCompactedOnLoad pin it); the newest maxEntries entries are returned, oldest first. maxEntries is at least 1 here: the app returns nothing for 0 without reading the file.",
  "function": "TranscriptStore.loadTail(maxEntries:) — input {file, maxEntries}: file the file's bytes (a string, or {\"hex\": <bytes>}), expected {texts, rewrite}: the texts of the entries returned, oldest first, and whether the file was rewritten",
  "verifiedBy": "DESIGN.md v1.6, v2.14; Tests/PowerUpTests/TranscriptFixtureTests.swift testTranscriptLoadTable writes the file to a temporary transcripts directory, loads it through TranscriptStore.loadTail and checks whether the bytes changed.",
  "capturedAgainst": "Swift 5.9.2 JSONDecoder, JSONEncoder and CryptoKit (Xcode 15.2) on macOS 27.2, PowerUp at 0bc961f",
  "cases": [
    {
      "name": "every entry of a short file, oldest first",
      "input": {
        "file": "{\"id\":\"3F2504E0-4F89-41D3-9A0C-0305E82C3301\",\"kind\":\"user\",\"text\":\"one\",\"date\":1761700000}\n{\"id\":\"3F2504E0-4F89-41D3-9A0C-0305E82C3301\",\"kind\":\"user\",\"text\":\"two\",\"date\":1761700000}\n{\"id\":\"3F2504E0-4F89-41D3-9A0C-0305E82C3301\",\"kind\":\"user\",\"text\":\"three\",\"date\":1761700000}\n",
        "maxEntries": 200
      },
      "expected": {
        "rewrite": false,
        "texts": [
          "one",
          "two",
          "three"
        ]
      },
      "reason": "A restore brings back the file's entries in the order they were written."
    },
    {
